<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick II, Grand Duke of Baden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1857–1928</span> · Also known as Friedrich II of Baden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick II was the last Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>, reigning from 1907 to 1918, the son of Frederick I and a grandson of Emperor William I. During the war he held a nominal army command. After a provisional government was formed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karlsruhe">Karlsruhe</a> in November 1918 he abdicated, and Baden became a democratic republic within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p></div>
